# Suite machine (plans 03-02..03-12): machine-level cases in one executable (D-15). Family
# sha256 (plan 03-02): core SHA-256 against independent literal digests, one case per line of
# data/sha256/vectors.txt plus the invariance, context and reset cases (D-28, A-04).
# Family create (plan 03-09): storage requirements, create, info and destroy through the public
# header, their refusals (whole-storage comparison), status names and the API version.
# Family digest (plan 03-09): the canonical state digest (D-35): literal streams, composite
# framing, field-table coverage, per-domain sensitivity, padding and the digest refusals.
# Plan 04-05 addition: machine.digest.stepped-literals pins the composite and domain 1..4
# digests of a stepped instance, recorded from the Phase 3 code (repeatability, A-03). Domains
# 16..18 (VIDEO, AUDIO, INPUT) are live: their sensitivity cases require that a row change moves
# only its own domain and never the composite (D-10), and the Phase 3 domain-16 refusal is
# retargeted to domain 19, the first value after them (plan 05-03: 19 is the live PSGLOG domain
# and the refusal moves to 20). machine.digest.video-fresh,
# machine.digest.composite-excludes-16-18 and machine.reset.clears-observation (in the digest
# family file) pin the fresh and reset observation rows and their separation from the composite.
# Plan 05-03 addition (composite version 2, PSG storage): machine.digest.composite-v2-framing,
# stream-instance-psg, domain-19-fresh, psg-rows-in-instance-domain, mem-rows-psg-regs, audio-rows,
# psglog-rows, cpu-images-independent-of-psg and machine.reset.psg-state-cleared.
# Family load (plan 03-10): typed EXEC, GROM and IVSC cartridge loads through the public header
# with generated stand-in bytes (D-24), their reports and digests, layer 2, the load options and
# unload back to the fresh state.
# Families refuse and prec (plan 03-11): the load refusal matrix, one id per row and prior
# (machine.refuse.load.<kind>.<slug>.<prior>, priors f fresh, x every other kind loaded, s EXEC
# and GROM loaded, c full), each asserting status, whole-storage memcmp, digest equality and the
# report detail fields (D-12); machine.prec.* pins each adjacent pair of the load ladder. The
# len-wrap rows (claimed length 2^32 + 8192) are skip-ok: they skip where size_t is 32 bits.
# Plan 03-11 addition: out parameters aimed into the instance (load report, info out, digest out,
# create out) are refused BAD_ARG with nothing written (machine.refuse.*.out-inside*,
# machine.refuse.load.*.report-inside.*). Review WR-01: that test runs only against a valid
# instance, after BAD_HANDLE (machine.refuse.digest.null-handle-low-out,
# machine.refuse.*.destroyed-out-inside, machine.refuse.load.exec.destroyed-report-inside).
# Review WR-02: an in struct's struct_size above IVS_STRUCT_SIZE_MAX (4096) is BAD_ARG before the
# unknown-tail scan; exactly 4096 keeps D-04 (machine.refuse.create.size-*,
# machine.create.size-at-max-ok, machine.refuse.load.exec.opts-{over-max,garbage-size,at-max-*}).
# Plan 06-04 (family stic.params): relation tests of the generated STIC parameter table over every registry
# profile: unit conversion, event table, window order, tiling within the frame, derived geometry, register file
# shape and the power-on record. The same plan extends machine.create.tables-cover-registry with the fourth table.
# Review WR-03: a damaged stored profile index (outside the registry, or the memory system's
# differing) makes the handle invalid: every handle-taking call is BAD_HANDLE on a relocated copy
# (machine.refuse.handle.*, family reset).
